# hextile

- Label: Hex Tile
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 10
- Parameters: 10 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/hextile.html
- Summary (EN): Randomly tiles a texture across large areas using hexagonal cells with random offsets. Each cell is randomly scaled and rotated, which avoids visible seams and obvious repetition.
- Résumé (FR) : Pave une texture de façon aléatoire sur de grandes surfaces grâce à des cellules hexagonales décalées, pivotées et mises à l'échelle au hasard.

- Inputs meaning: ["direction: orients tiles, for example along curve tangents", "texcoord: custom texture coordinates for mapping", "textotile: the texture to tile", "size, scale, rot: per-tile size, scale and rotation multipliers", "contrast, contrast_falloff, weightexp: blend contrast, falloff and weight multipliers"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Size", "meaning": "tile size in canvas XY coordinates"}, {"name": "Scale / Rotate", "meaning": "global scale and rotation of the tiles"}, {"name": "Scale Random / Rotate Random", "meaning": "random per-cell variation"}, {"name": "Random Seed", "meaning": "changes the random arrangement"}, {"name": "Contrast", "meaning": "contrast between blended cells"}, {"name": "Falloff", "meaning": "contrast falloff between cells; 0 gives a hard transition"}, {"name": "Weight Exp", "meaning": "exponential weighting of transition areas"}]

- Caveats: ["By default the node uses canvas XY coordinates; supplying texcoord changes the mapping.", "Where a direction vector has zero length, the default orientation set by Rotate and Rotate Random is used."]

